KG42.register("clusters-b6e68bb07c97b45623cd706c",{"id":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v142-d-K001","paper":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading","label":"Cooperative welfare dispatch, common tariff, and linear settlement","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Cooperative welfare dispatch, common tariff, and linear settlement","market_meaning":"Under the condition that customers cooperate jointly and the dispatch belongs to their respective feasible sets, the aggregator provides the information required for sequential dispatch; the welfare-optimal dispatch corresponds to customer optimal subproblems through a common marginal-cost tariff, and that tariff forms customer bills and the aggregator's procurement-payment obligation.","mechanism_ids":["M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"All chains belong to a deterministic cooperative mechanism. The sequential-solution information of P1_i and the optimal-tariff representation of P2_i are retained separately; the wholesale price function and the common retail tariff are not treated as the same quantity, and the billing conclusion is limited to the stated optimal linear tariff.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Assembled according to the actual dependencies among the welfare objective, information input, tariff implementation and billing. EV electricity-selling eligibility forms another cluster; this cluster cannot yet serve as an executable algorithm containing all physical constraints and iteration details.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the welfare objective, cost definition, and the correspondence between the optimal common tariff and the customer subproblems."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Provide the aggregated net energy consumption of others used for sequential scheduling and the aggregator's broadcast responsibility."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Clarify the aggregator's setting and uniform application of the rate, as well as the coordination activity in which customers obtain information round by round."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Apply the optimal common rate to customer bills, and retain the conclusion that the procurement payment obligation and the bill cover the cost."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Xneg-i","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e04"],"rationale":"The source lists the aggregated net energy consumption of others as an input to P1_i; R002 defines the broadcast content, and R001 describes that this information serves welfare scheduling; the interface does not add scientific edges."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04"],"rationale":"The same information exchange passage supports the aggregator updating the broadcast and the customer obtaining information respectively; the two Rule-Chains complement the sending responsibility and the received content, and are not duplicate rules or new graph relations."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pi"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E16"],"rationale":"The optimal common rate given by the proposition is uniformly applied by the aggregator to the customer subproblem; this connection is limited to the rate representation at the optimum, and does not derive a round-by-round rate update algorithm."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"The source explicitly uses the announced and uniformly applied rate for billing by time-period net energy, so coordination and settlement have a direct functional linkage."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pi","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-tot"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pi-star-t","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-i-tot-star","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"Settlement uses the net energy and common rate at the welfare-optimal dispatch. The interface from general dispatch quantity to optimal billing quantity is one that takes the optimal instance, and it does not rewrite the two local roles as the same decision object."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"The same M01 aggregator undertakes broadcast, rate implementation, and payment duties, and only the node display is unified; the duties of each Rule-Chain and the original objects continue to be retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e04"],"rationale":"These references carry the price coordination function of the same collaboration mechanism. Node display normalization is not equivalent to merging the wholesale price function, the optimal common rate, or different information steps."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-tot","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-i-tot"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e03"],"rationale":"The source definition and sequential update formula show that both refer to customer time-period net energy. The scheduling role of R001 and the iterative snapshot and aggregate input roles of R002 are retained separately, and values in different rounds are not deemed equal."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pi","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pi-star-t"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"The two correspond to the common rate at the same optimal dispatch in Equation (9); the rate variable role of R001 and the billing parameter role of R005 are retained, and objects are not rewritten across fields."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-a","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-a-t"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"The time-varying slope of the same M01 wholesale price function enters the objective cost, the optimal rate, and the settlement identity respectively; the parameter references of each Rule-Chain are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-b","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-b-t"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"The time-varying intercept of the same M01 wholesale price function is used in the two Rule-Chains, and the identity is supported by the common definition and the applicable mechanism; the local parameter objects are retained separately."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G01","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The frozen Rule-Chain references customer feasibility via X_i, but does not provide complete appliance, net energy, EV charging and discharging, and battery state constraint objects; the physical feasibility of dispatch cannot be checked from this cluster.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-app","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-tot"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should supplement a complete citable feasibility Rule-Chain and battery state definition, while D keeps the existing objective and feasible set references unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The current Rule-Chain does not retain the complete P1_i solution update; the aggregated broadcast quantity mixes data updated in the current round and data not updated in the previous round, while the procedure only states that a broadcast occurs at the start of each round, and the recalculation timing within the customer sequence is not yet clear. Equation (9) also cannot directly serve as the current iterative rate update formula.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Supplement the sequential customer solution Rule-Chain and clarify the granularity of the broadcast timing; express separately the steps of solving the welfare-optimal dispatch and computing the common rate at the optimum."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The wholesale input price and the marginal-cost common rate still depend on the existing coordination and settlement nodes; the related node proposals have not yet been approved, and the two types of prices cannot be equated because of display normalization.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-p","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pi","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pi-star-t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P01","v141-b-g02-p03"],"required_work":"Manual inspection should examine the proposal boundary and whether the ontology needs to be expanded; before approval, the existing node, parameter, and variable references are retained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B material referenced by this cluster remains unverified, and is used only for candidate assembly under the experimental policy; it has not been confirmed by an independent source or scientific review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently check the original source and transcription item by item, retaining the current candidate eligibility and source status."}]},"rule_refs":["38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R001","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R002","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R003","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R005"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-76d88cced26fe0a5","COMP-ebacec241379c91d","COMP-ee664d90be53dd00","KG40-88d16cf517d0bffb"]});
